{"redo_desc_about":"Are you looking for a fun and tasty way to explore the local craft drinks scene? Join us on a Wine, beer and gin tour and discover the wineries, breweries and distilleries in the Barossa.

You'll get to sample a variety of wine, beers and gins, learn about the history and techniques of the makers, and enjoy a delicious Pizza for lunch.

Whether you're a wine lover, beer lover, a gin enthusiast, or just curious about the art of brewing and distilling, you'll find something to suit your palate and your mood. Book your wine, beer and gin tour today and get ready for an unforgettable experience!","redo_desc_highlights":"","redo_desc_what_included":"Winery tour with our driver and guide!","redo_desc_what_excluded":"","redo_desc_itinerary":"","redo_desc_what_to_bring":"","redo_desc_duration_text":"8 Hours","redo_desc_requirements":"","redo_desc_cancellation":"","redo_desc_check_in":"Pickup times will be from 8:45am - 9:45am depending on location of pick up. We will let you know prior to the booking time.","redo_desc_faqs":"","redo_min_age":"","redo_max_age":"","redo_group_size":"6","redo_meeting_point":"Your hotel or pick up location","redo_desc_other":""}

{"redo_desc_about":"Set sail on a one-of-a-kind adventure where cosmic mystery meets breathtaking scenery! Our UFO Festival Boat Tour invites you to drift through the region's most stunning waterways while uncovering the legends of unexplained sightings that have made this area a hotspot for UFO enthusiasts worldwide.

As we cruise along tranquil Hinchinbrook Channel and winding rivers, you'll be surrounded by awe-inspiring natural beauty of Hinchinbrook Islands landscapes—towering forests, mirror-like water, and dramatic skies that seem tailor-made for a close encounter. Our expert guides will share riveting stories of strange lights, eerie encounters, and local legends tied to real UFO sightings that have puzzled residents and researchers for decades.

Whether you're a believer, a skeptic, or just in it for the views, this tour offers something truly out of this world. Soak in the beauty. Watch the skies. You never know what might appear just over the treetops…","redo_desc_highlights":"","redo_desc_what_included":"A selection of cold drinks","redo_desc_what_excluded":"","redo_desc_itinerary":"","redo_desc_what_to_bring":"BYO alcohol","redo_desc_duration_text":"1.5 hours","redo_desc_requirements":"","redo_desc_cancellation":"","redo_desc_check_in":"","redo_desc_faqs":"","redo_min_age":"","redo_max_age":"","redo_group_size":"","redo_meeting_point":"Cardwell Jetty – Please note: Location may change depending on weather conditions","redo_desc_other":""}

{"redo_desc_about":"Frequently referred to as one of New Zealand's most spectacular destinations, Omanawa Falls is situated in the stunning Kaimai ranges. At its heart featuring a breathtaking 35m waterfall cascading into a pristine pool surrounded by lush New Zealand native rainforest. Kaitiaki Adventures will lead you on an unparalleled, culturally integral, and historic guided walk that immerses you in the rich cultural history of the Ngati Hangarau people. A regenerative tourism experience in the unique cultural space of Omanawa Falls.

Join our friendly, knowledgeable local guides through the beautiful trails to 2 lookouts, the Māori carvings, the century old hydro electric power station service tunnel and the breathtaking Omanawa falls. Departing Omanawa falls follows a visit to McLaren Falls and Tauranga's best view point the Minden Lookout.

Immerse yourself in the surrounding flora and fauna while listening to the stories of the area, the Awa (River), and the cultural values of mana whenua.","redo_desc_highlights":"","redo_desc_what_included":"","redo_desc_what_excluded":"","redo_desc_itinerary":"","redo_desc_what_to_bring":"","redo_desc_duration_text":"2.5 Hours","redo_desc_requirements":"","redo_desc_cancellation":"","redo_desc_check_in":"","redo_desc_faqs":"","redo_min_age":"","redo_max_age":"","redo_group_size":"","redo_meeting_point":"Omanawa Falls & Mt Maunganui, New Zealand","redo_desc_other":""}

{"redo_desc_about":"#Welcome to The FLUID Project! The ultimate creative space to re-awaken your inner child!

Our guided fluid art workshops are available 7 days a week - perfect for your big birthday bash, hens nights, corporate team bonding, or more! If you need a custom event type or more people to attend, please don't hesitate to let us know. We are able to cater for up to 40 people with notice!

The FLUID Project is Australia's newest EPIC creative experience. Nestled in a concrete warehouse, we have built a space to allow you to unleash your creativity and express your emotions on our variety of mediums. Popularised on TikTok and Instagram, and perfect for your next date day/night, come and share a connective and immersive experience with that special someone or share a fun memorable experience with your family or your friends. The FLUID Project is all about creativity, connectivity and community! Come and see what the hype is about as you paint your own Fluid Bear or Canvas.","redo_desc_highlights":"","redo_desc_what_included":"","redo_desc_what_excluded":"","redo_desc_itinerary":"","redo_desc_what_to_bring":"We cover you with an apron, but you may get a little messy! Don't wear your super nice clothes and shoes. We recommend keeping it casual with no droopy long sleeves.","redo_desc_duration_text":"1.5 - 2 hours","redo_desc_requirements":"","redo_desc_cancellation":"","redo_desc_check_in":"","redo_desc_faqs":"","redo_min_age":"","redo_max_age":"","redo_group_size":"","redo_meeting_point":"","redo_desc_other":"If cash is king for you and you'd like to pay in cash, please contact us and we will book you in for a cash session! $30 deposit per person applies, you can pay over the phone."}

