{"redo_desc_about":"A scenic watertaxi from Halfmoon Bay Wharf to Ulva Island to explore the crown jewel of the Rakiura National Park - this is a Bird Sanctuary Island with endemic species and pristine forests protected from invasive pests.","redo_desc_highlights":"Departure from Halfmoon Bay Wharf to Ulva Island is a longer boat ride than from Golden Bay Wharf, it is a more scenic ride with points of interest along the way: Ackers Point - The Light House, The Ringaringa Passage (where sealions like to hang-out), Harold's Bay (the second oldest stone cottage in New Zealand).","redo_desc_what_included":"A small introductory talk is given when arriving at Ulva Island to help orient you and give you an estimate of how long it takes to walk the tracks and things to watch out for.","redo_desc_what_excluded":"One cannot buy provisions on Ulva Island, please bring your own food and drink and adequate clothing.","redo_desc_itinerary":"","redo_desc_what_to_bring":"Please bring adequate footwear and clothing, and your own food and drink.","redo_desc_duration_text":"20 minutes","redo_desc_requirements":"Children must be accompanied by an adult. Please do not feed the wildlife, and take your rubbish back with you.

